Sval: serve Sval's own filter lists to the content classifier

List ids that start with "sval-" are lists Sval downloads from each publisher
(protections spec §1.2). The Remote Settings client is
the object the content classifier asks for list bytes, so it hands those ids
to SvalBlockingLists, and hands it the service so that a list Sval refreshes
rebuilds its engine. Mozilla's lists still come from Remote Settings.

The client is a singleton registered by contract id in Mozilla's
components.conf; replacing it would mean copying the whole client.

